    <item>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mastodon.jakewharton.com/@jw/117094650221420536</guid>
      <link>https://mastodon.jakewharton.com/@jw/117094650221420536</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:49:28 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;As of today, the Lysine projects (OkHttp, Okio, Retrofit, and the SQL Delight family) have a contribution policy that forbids LLM usage for creating code and for PR/issue descriptions and comments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is an exception for translation assistance provided you disclose its use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you choose to use LLMs locally for research, analysis, and/or experimentation we can't stop you. But for contributing we require &lt;u&gt;you&lt;/u&gt; to write the code, and for our interactions to be with &lt;u&gt;you&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
